ce3f8479a19b3","github_link":"https://github.com/andremichelle/openDAW/commit/5108377cc60d03c32f8406fa870ce3f8479a19b3","commit_subject":"The Arpeggio has 18 walk modes instead of 3 (Up, Down and UpDown stay first), an Order choice between played and pitch order, Hold, Retrigger (off, note, bar or beat of the time signature), Offset, a Seed with a dice to reseed, and a 64-step sequencer with rest, tie and chord steps plus velocity, gate, pitch, octave, chance and ratchet lanes. Every played note keeps the cents of the held note it comes from (#526). Projects and presets made before play exactly as they did: Mode automation and Mode modulation are converted to the new list of modes, and automation shared with another parameter is copied first. The Delay migration converts its rate automation now, which it never did, and presets are migrated on load like projects. MIDI effects split by automation updates no longer see a transport jump twice in one block, so a loop wrap no longer cuts the first arpeggio note short. Devices can ask the engine for the bar at a position.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"dimagi/open-chat-studio","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:20:21Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"a0cf9944c81317c9ea00c1f02d0779a28be275db","github_link":"https://github.com/dimagi/open-chat-studio/commit/a0cf9944c81317c9ea00c1f02d0779a28be275db","commit_subject":"feat(pipelines): show an archived chatbot's graph in its read-only builder","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"comet-ml/opik","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:20:09Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"4d3b22160c5b8acc243ef1977d5116da83f4e9e7","github_link":"https://github.com/comet-ml/opik/commit/4d3b22160c5b8acc243ef1977d5116da83f4e9e7","commit_subject":"[OPIK-9029] [BE] fix: tolerate a span id in more than one project in SpanDAO.getById (#9311)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"yuzutech/kroki","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:20:03Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"ffd7e6e650c7c554a6e115bcb5d5ada693152e5c","github